course: dictionary
lesson: 5885
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one is right. «He tries his grand old manner, "I'm well-known in these parts", but the clerk laughs at the "madam"» shows manner as the way a person behaves and speaks. Toad is showing off, so manner means how he acts.
explain: Ask yourself: is the word talking about how something is done, or how someone behaves? In «Mind your manners at the table», manner means polite behaviour, like saying please and thank you. Then swap your meaning into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
explain: Watch for set phrases. «All manner of» means all kinds of, so «all manner of toys» means every kind of toy. A phrase like «table manners» is a fixed pair of words that you learn together, not one word at a time.
fact: Manner is a noun. Manners is the plural form, used for polite behaviour.
fact: «Manner» can mean the way something is done, such as «quickly» or «slowly».
fact: «Manners» means polite ways of behaving, such as saying please and thank you.
fact: «All manner of» means all kinds of.
fact: Adverbs of manner tell how something is done, such as «quickly», «slowly» or «quietly».
exercise: «She greeted us in a friendly manner.» What does manner mean here? | The time of day | A room for guests | A small bag | *The way she behaved towards us
exercise: «Mind your manners at the dinner table.» What does manners mean? | Dinner plates and cups | Long, dull rules about school | *Polite ways of behaving, like saying please | Loud games and running
exercise: In «She walked quickly», which word is an adverb of manner, telling how she walked? | the | walked | *quickly | she
test: «There were all manner of toys in the shop.» What does all manner of mean? | *All kinds of | Hidden | Broken | Only one
test: In «He tries his grand old manner», what does manner mean? | A type of cake | A door of the house | *The way he behaves and speaks | A bag of coins
exam: In which sentence does manner mean the way something is done? | «Good table manners make dinner pleasant.» | «All manner of birds sang in the trees.» | *«She opened the box in a careful manner.»
